 was written and developed by ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"t4jsp6waAw"},{"type":"link","url":"https://beatriznegreiros.com/","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Beatriz Negreiros","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"MZS6pq59VZ"}],"urlSource":"https://beatriznegreiros.com/","key":"TAvCHOHGk1"},{"type":"text","value":" ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"PPe9f5js1H"},{"type":"image","url":"/build/beatriz-7823673b7e6cf2f0f85b73b457caad97.jpg","alt":"Beatriz Negreiros","width":50,"height":50,"key":"wfRuc2O0hR","urlSource":"../img/authors/beatriz.jpg"}],"key":"JfZ5o14oFd"}],"class":"tip","key":"YCCfCCVo14"},{"type":"heading","depth":1,"position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Introduction","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"Br9qE8OSro"}],"label":"machinelearning","identifier":"machinelearning","html_id":"machinelearning","key":"c9esqZhT9H"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Machine learning (ML) is arguably one of the most prominent tools in data science to advance water resources research. ML models are capable of learning complex underlying relationships of a system, and thus finds its applications in various water resources topics: from river ecosystems to water supply. We will cover a variety of learning algorithms and methods to optimize ML models so that they can generalize to unseen data, which will include in principle supervised and unsupervised learning techniques.","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"plKREtKfWv"}],"key":"Lm5ZZXD1D1"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The goal of machine learning","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"CI3BhmXL0K"}],"identifier":"the-goal-of-machine-learning","label":"The goal of machine learning","html_id":"the-goal-of-machine-learning","implicit":true,"key":"MkASgSxktO"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Machine learning aims at computationally learning complex relationships from experience (i.e., data). ","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"J1E8uYxkBJ"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Computational learning","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"O2025nJ9O8"}],"key":"qLRHHScYfD"},{"type":"text","value":" is a subfield of artificial intelligence (AI) that focuses on the development of models that enable computers to learn and make predictions or decisions without being explicitly programmed. It involves designing and implementing mathematical and statistical models that can automatically analyze data, identify patterns, and make informed decisions or predictions based on the observed data. This task may be, for instance, predicting or modelling complex phenomena. Note that predicting here does not refer only to the future but to any non-identified event. For instance, we can predict whether a chemical substance will be, or was, or is, dissolved in water given a set of environmental conditions.","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"lUMy0IeiOc"}],"key":"c7w7snzhpk"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contrary to popular thinking, ML algorithms have been around for several decades. However, they were only given stark attention in the last decade when limitations in computing power were no longer an obstacle for applying ML ","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"DZs1USHGkn"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"algorithms","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"L97p5Snw7n"}],"key":"a9DDtaEFfM"},{"type":"text","value":" for making helpful ","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"MQOrsT2YVQ"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"ML models","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"iBzcfzZbHm"}],"key":"jseH4eXeyf"},{"type":"text","value":". We refer to ","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"ee0fCP7Clj"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"algorithms","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"tswCJ8jgqy"}],"key":"o7fMM0icqc"},{"type":"text","value":" as the baseline commands that instruct a model ","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"Bu2fAkqbPy"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"how to learn","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"TNvCPhCQ6w"}],"key":"vGwxtre180"},{"type":"text","value":" from data, whereas a ","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"G8XPbDWEIi"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"ML model","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"e